WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.400
About 100,000 households around Keeve lost internet after Russian strikes that killed four. This

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:12.820
is Omni View Europe, episode four. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host. On Friday,

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:17.940
a Russian drone hit the Incom Business Center in the capital. Ukrainian officials said the

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:22.880
building held a data group data center, and that the strike damaged it. Data Group said

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:28.580
service kept running from backup sites. President Volodomir Zelensky said Moscow had pushed

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:33.760
the attacks onto data centers and internet providers to disrupt ordinary life as much as it could.

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:39.520
He said people are losing the means to stay in touch, to study and to work. Russia said it hit

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:44.960
the site because Ukrainian military intelligence was using it. The Russian Defense Ministry confirmed

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:52.020
the data group strike and said its forces also targeted new telco, United DC, Keave Star, and Parkovie,

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:58.420
while strikes on energy and rail continued. The times of India, citing the BBC and Ukrainian officials,

00:00:58.580 --> 00:01:01.980
reported damage at data centers run by key internet providers.

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:07.640
Across the region, the European Commission wants labels on how data centers use energy and water,

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:11.700
cypress male reports, for sites of 500 kilowatts or more.

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:14.540
Operators would report those efficiency figures,

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:17.340
how their water use sits against local water stress,

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:19.380
and whether they can help the local grid,

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:21.440
including by reusing waste heat.

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:24.820
The plan sets no ceiling on electricity or water,

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:28.160
and it does not make operators publish total power used.

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:34.880
European Union figures put these sites at about 2.5% of EU electricity. Combined capacity

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:41.380
is expected to rise from 12 gigawatts last year to 28 by 2030. And the Union wants capacity

00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:46.660
tripled within seven years. Governments and lawmakers have two months to object. If they

00:01:46.660 --> 00:01:51.420
do not, the rules take effect. And the labels could later be required before any binding

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:59.140
minimum standards. In the Paris region, Matthew, Hyde, and colleagues plotted 28,349 cardiac

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:05.820
arrests outside hospital from 2011 through 2024, leaving out central Paris. They set those

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:13.460
cases against 1,893 fixed to fibrillators. Hillary Minka, the first author, said only 30 percent

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:20.100
were within 500 meters of the nearest recorded device, the Guardian reports. 910 more fixed machines

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:23.980
would put 84.5% of those cases inside that distance.

00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:27.320
1,712 would cover all of them.

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:31.200
Drones working inside a radius of 3,900 meters

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:33.400
could lift coverage with fewer devices.

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:36.520
In the United Kingdom, the British Heart Foundation

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:40.180
counts more than 30,000 out of hospital cardiac arrests a year

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:42.480
in which crews try to restart the heart.

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:44.880
Fewer than one in ten people survive

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:49.540
and each minute without CPR and a shock cuts that chance by 10%.

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:54.780
Also today, Finland and Sweden made their first joint intercept of Russian jets over the

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:57.120
Gulf of Finland, the Kiev Indicendant Reports.

